"""Verified supertree generator for arXiv:1210.3762.

The paper studies compatibility of profiles of unrooted phylogenetic trees.
This module inverse-generates a compatible profile by first choosing a binary
caterpillar supertree and then distributing its edge splits among unresolved
input trees.  The planted answer is the supertree itself, in standard Newick
notation.  Verification never reads that answer: it parses and validates the
submitted tree and checks, by exact split containment, that it displays every
input tree.

All input trees have the full taxon set.  Thus the split transformation cited
in Section 1 and the Splits Equivalence Theorem used in Section 4 give a
polynomial reference algorithm.  This is consequently an honest Track-B
family, not a claim that these planted instances inherit worst-case
NP-completeness.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import hashlib
import json
import math
import os
import random
import re
import sys
